## Nmap scan type differences (TCP / SYN / FIN)

| Scan | How it detects open port | Reliability | Stealth | Needs sudo |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `-sT` (Connect) | Full 3-way handshake completes | Very reliable | None (fully logged) | No |
| `-sS` (SYN) | SYN-ACK received, then RST sent (never completes) | Reliable | Moderate (half-open) | Yes |
| `-sF` (FIN) | No response to FIN = open; RST = closed | Less reliable (ambiguous) | High (evades basic filters) | Yes |

Note: `-sF` doesn't work reliably against Windows targets — Windows doesn't follow the expected RFC behavior.

