## Nessus setup gotchas

- Must use `https://localhost:8834` — not `http://` (you'll get a "Bad Request" otherwise)
- Browser will warn "not secure" (self-signed cert) — click Advanced → Proceed anyway
- Choose **Nessus Essentials** (free, register at tenable.com/products/nessus/nessus-essentials with name+email → emailed activation code)
- If the install wizard only shows paid tiers (Expert/Professional/Manager) with no Essentials option: select any option on that screen, then paste your free Essentials activation code when prompted — the code itself determines your actual tier, regardless of what was clicked

**`sudo dpkg -i Nessus-*.deb`**
- `dpkg` = Debian's low-level package installer (installs a local .deb file directly, no internet dependency resolution like `apt`)
- `-i` = install flag
- `Nessus-*.deb` = wildcard matching the actual versioned filename
- If it errors "cannot access archive" — check `ls ~/Downloads`, the file is probably there, not in your current folder. Also make sure it's an actual `.deb` file, not an accidentally-extracted folder (a `.deb` should show as a single file icon, not a folder with DEBIAN/opt subfolders)

